## Test Anti-Pattern Audit: `ProductCatalogTests.cs`

### Summary

| Severity | Count |
|----------|-------|
| **Critical** | **2** |
| **High** | 0 |
| **Medium** | 1 |
| **Low** | 1 |

This test suite is a textbook **coverage-touching** class. All 10 public methods of `ProductCatalog` are called, which explains the 95% coverage number, but **7 of 10 tests verify nothing meaningful**. Bugs in price calculation, CSV formatting, search logic, deletion, and import parsing would all slip through undetected.

---

### Critical Findings

#### 1. Coverage-Touching Pattern (Systemic — 7 tests)

Every public method is invoked in declaration order with no real assertion. This is the #1 reason bugs escape to production.

| Test Method | What It Does | What It Should Verify |
|---|---|---|
| `AddProduct_Works` (L17) | Calls `AddProduct` — no assertion | Product is retrievable afterward |
| `UpdatePrice_Works` (L32) | Calls `UpdatePrice` — no assertion | Price changed to new value |
| `RemoveProduct_Works` (L39) | Calls `RemoveProduct` — no assertion | Product is no longer retrievable |
| `GetProductCount_Works` (L63) | Calls `GetProductCount` — no assertion | Count equals expected value |
| `ApplyBulkDiscount_Works` (L68) | Calls `ApplyBulkDiscount` — no assertion | Each product's price reduced by 10% |
| `ImportFromCsv_Works` (L85) | Calls `ImportFromCsv` — no assertion | Parsed product is in store with correct fields |

**Fix example — `AddProduct_Works`:**
```csharp
// BEFORE — proves nothing
[TestMethod]
public void AddProduct_Works()
{
    var product = new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m);
    _catalog.AddProduct(product);
}

// AFTER — verifies the product was actually stored
[TestMethod]
public void AddProduct_ProductIsRetrievable()
{
    var product = new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m);
    _catalog.AddProduct(product);

    var retrieved = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
    Assert.AreEqual("Widget", retrieved?.Name);
    Assert.AreEqual(9.99m, retrieved?.Price);
}
```

**Fix example — `ApplyBulkDiscount_Works`:**
```csharp
// BEFORE — 10% discount could compute to anything
[TestMethod]
public void ApplyBulkDiscount_Works()
{
    _catalog.AddProduct(new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m));
    _catalog.AddProduct(new Product("SKU-002", "Gadget", 19.99m));
    _catalog.ApplyBulkDiscount(0.10m);
}

